"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786750489998803001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"551e9e81-76d7-4b4b-b7e3-5d613c438410","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4f50-b1f2-78af-4326"}],"description":"## Context\nOrganic Gerrit Verify run 31846417650 emitted 260 fixture_setup spans over 1 second totaling 380.393 aggregate worker-seconds. Excluding the separately proven 35-second editor DNS delay, the largest module totals were: tests/unit/test_secret_screen_e7a9.py 28.998s / 23 setups; tests/interfaces/queries/test_list_filters.py 25.856s / 17; tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py 19.230s / 7; tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py 16.486s / 11; and tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py 12.846s / 9. Closed precedent peculiar-calmy-bubblefish proved that a session template plus isolated per-test copies reduced tests/interfaces wall time from 270.7s to 186.5s (31%) while running nine more tests, and explicitly deferred roughly 20 module-local fixtures as the larger remaining win.\n\n## Phase 1 plan\n- Trace each measured >1s setup to its exact fixture and separate from-scratch git/rebar store initialization, fixture copying/fix-up, test-body work, and runner variance with setup-only timing plus runtime instrumentation.\n- Test the dynamic hypothesis that the five modules repeatedly build equivalent virgin git-backed stores. Confirm only where the same initialized precondition recurs; reject template reuse for fixtures whose setup semantics intentionally vary or whose contract is initialization itself.\n- Search ticket history for prior acceptance/rejection and compare the remediation with at least three popular, actively maintained OSS projects using session-scoped expensive templates with isolated per-test copy/reset. Apply the parent ticket consensus rule: at least two-thirds use the practice and none documents rejecting it for coverage/reliability.\n\n## Phase 2 plan (only after confirmed RCA and consensus)\n- Add or extend one uniquely named test helper at an existing call-graph seam; use session/worker-local templates and per-test copies only for confirmed equivalent fixtures.\n- Preserve the safety contracts established by peculiar-calmy-bubblefish: rewrite both linked-worktree pointers, reject bare git worktree repair, allocate a per-test gate snapshot directory, regenerate environment/signing identity, reset module caches, keep the template virgin, and retain deliberate from-scratch initialization/recovery tests.\n- Prove RED->GREEN with durable isolation sentinels before migrating consumers. Do not remove, skip, sample, xfail, or weaken any behavioral assertion.\n- Run every affected module, full owning tiers, the full default/integration selectors, lint, typecheck, and workflow guards. Measure paired before/after setup and wall time under the same environment and report runner-seconds saved without claiming critical-path savings from aggregate fixture time.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every targeted setup is attributed to a specific fixture operation with a focused measured baseline.\n- [ ] The confirmed RCA includes a runtime experiment that discriminates repeated equivalent store construction from test-body work and unavoidable per-test semantics.\n- [ ] Tracker history and at least three popular actively maintained OSS projects are cited; consensus is evaluated by the parent rule.\n- [ ] Only fixtures proven equivalent are migrated; initialization/recovery contracts continue to build from scratch.\n- [ ] Collected/passed test counts and all pre-existing assertions are preserved or increased.\n- [ ] Per-test copies cannot share ticket refs, linked-worktree paths, gate snapshots, environment IDs, signing keys, module caches, or mutable config state.\n- [ ] Durable sentinels fail for stale half-rewritten pointers, bare worktree repair, shared refs, shared identity/signing state, and non-virgin templates.\n- [ ] A defect-seeded mutation of each newly relied-on isolation fix returns the relevant sentinel to RED.\n- [ ] Paired before/after setup and module/tier wall-time measurements quantify runner-seconds saved.\n- [ ] Full affected tiers plus default/integration selectors, lint, typecheck, and workflow guards pass.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change receives LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and merges before closure.\n\n## Back-out\nRevert the Gerrit change to restore per-test from-scratch fixture construction; no product behavior or coverage destination changes.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/_store_template.py","reason":"extend the proven isolated store-clone seam only if the confirmed fixtures can reuse it safely"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/conftest.py","reason":"expose any worker-local template fixture needed by measured interface modules"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_secret_screen_e7a9.py","reason":"migrate or retain the measured 23 from-scratch setups according to the RCA"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/queries/test_list_filters.py","reason":"replace repeated equivalent pre-seeded scenario construction if the runtime experiment confirms it"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py","reason":"two_clones fixture source used by the measured rebuild-history module"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py","reason":"measured seven repeated two-clone setups and regression coverage"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py","reason":"measured eleven repeated equivalent git-graph setups"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py","reason":"measured nine repeated origin plus store setups"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py","reason":"extend durable template isolation sentinels if shared helper behavior changes"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","performance","pytest","fixtures","debug"],"ticket_id":"41d2-2814-a368-4c79","ticket_type":"task","title":"Eliminate repeated git-store construction in measured long-pole fixtures","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f0203100-6bf8-4390-bbb8-2f689b3c3d40","2f50f09a-7f7a-4a1c-a078-6985f1e0d895","551e9e81-76d7-4b4b-b7e3-5d613c438410"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786750548256310002,"uuid":"bb6062a8-1774-4c77-bfdd-fc679a477b3d"}